### Evidence class
C. Structural Robustness

### Question

Does the spectral structure of the canonical morphology
representation remain stable when complete provenance-defined
replication groups are removed?

### Canonical reference

Morphology matrix:
2300 × 135

Frozen replication structure:

- 230 replication groups
- Group sizes: 9–11 observations
- 224 groups of size 10
- 3 groups of size 9
- 3 groups of size 11

Canonical spectral reference:

- D80 = 32
- D90 = 53
- D95 = 73
- D99 = 108
- Effective dimension ≈ 10.549
- PC01 variance ≈ 0.28253

### Resampling design

Complete replication groups were removed as the
perturbation unit.

Conditions:

- 5 groups removed
- 10 groups removed
- 20 groups removed

Replicates:

20 per condition

Total spectral fits:

60

For every replicate:

1. complete replication groups were removed;
2. PCA was recomputed independently;
3. spectral dimensions were measured;
4. effective dimensionality was measured;
5. eigenvalue structure was compared with the canonical spectrum;
6. leading eigenspace alignment was measured.

Replication labels were used **only to define the perturbation
unit**, not to discover morphology structure.

