## E07 — Within-Region Morphology Coherence

### Evidence class
A. Morphology Geometry → Density-Region Structure

### Question

Are independently discovered density regions internally
morphologically coherent?

---

### Input

Intrinsic morphology:

2300 × 73

Density-basin matrix:

2300 × 6

Observational scales:

6

Basin assignments:

frozen from the density-ascent analysis.

No basin was redefined for this analysis.

---

### Primary test

For each observational scale:

    within-basin morphology distance

was compared with:

    between-basin morphology distance.

Secondary evidence:

    local-neighbor retention within basin boundaries.

---

### Results

| Scale | Basins | Within mean | Between mean | Within/Between | Local retention |
|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| 4.707252 | 7 | 14.498 | 13.549 | 1.070 | 0.755 |
| 5.416895 | 6 | 14.399 | 13.623 | 1.057 | 0.774 |
| 6.248407 | 5 | 14.300 | 13.710 | 1.043 | 0.804 |
| 7.596034 | 7 | 14.307 | 13.678 | 1.046 | 0.804 |
| 10.640832 | 7 | 14.222 | 13.678 | 1.040 | 0.843 |
| 16.568532 | 8 | 14.332 | 13.338 | 1.075 | 0.845 |

---

### Primary finding

The within-basin morphology distances were NOT smaller
than between-basin distances.

Instead:

    within / between ≈ 1.04–1.07

across all six scales.

Therefore the density basins should NOT be described as
strongly compact morphology clusters.

---

### Secondary finding

Local-neighbor retention within basins increased with scale:

    0.755
    0.774
    0.804
    0.804
    0.843
    0.845

This indicates that a substantial fraction of local morphology
neighbors remain within the same density basin, with stronger
retention at the larger observational scales.

However, the basin-level global distance contrast remains weak.

---

### Scientific interpretation

The appropriate interpretation is:

> Density basins represent recurring regions of the morphology
> density landscape, but they do not correspond to strongly
> compact morphology clusters under the intrinsic Euclidean
> distance measure.

The evidence therefore favors:

    continuous morphology geometry
            +
    recurring density concentrations
            +
    substantial local basin coherence

rather than:

    discrete, well-separated morphology classes.

---

### Important distinction

